# Copy to .env and fill in for local development.
# These are read into app.json's `extra` block via app.config.js — see
# docs/mobile-architecture.md for how expo-constants picks them up.

# Base URL of the existing Node/Express backend's REST API (no trailing slash).
# For local development leave it at localhost: when this points at localhost or a LAN IP, the app swaps
# in the address of the machine it was loaded from (the browser page's host on the web, the Metro dev
# server's host on a phone/emulator - see src/config/env.ts). Switching Wi-Fi then needs no edit here.
# The phone and the machine running the backend must be on the same network.
# For an EAS production/preview build this MUST be the backend's real public HTTPS URL (e.g.
# https://api.yourdomain.com/api/v1), set as an EAS environment variable/secret before building -
# a real server URL is always used as-is.
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000/api/v1

# MapLibre-compatible style JSON — must be a real OSM-derived basemap (roads,
# buildings, labels, water/land), not a Google Maps style/service.
#
# Default: OpenFreeMap's "Liberty" style — a free, key-free, globally-covering
# OSM vector basemap (OpenMapTiles schema) maintained specifically for
# MapLibre use (https://openfreemap.org). No signup, no secret to protect.
# DO NOT use https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json here — that is
# MapLibre's own minimal test style (a flat background fill with no real
# road/building/label data anywhere in the world) and is dev/demo-only; it is
# exactly what produced the "blank light-blue map" bug this fixes.
#
# Alternatives if OpenFreeMap's fair-use policy or coverage doesn't suit a
# future deployment (e.g. MapTiler, Stadia Maps) require an API key — put it
# directly in this URL's query string (client-safe "public"/map-display keys
# only; never a server-side Google Maps key here, see README "Geocoding").
MAP_STYLE_URL=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty

# Optional: OSRM (or compatible) road-routing engine base URL, if the backend
# does not already return road-network polylines in the route response.
OSRM_BASE_URL=
